I added a conformance case, 'Disabled 8b', to /mnt/d/Profile/Users/Tushar/Documents/GIT/MultiMeters/tests/test_disabled.lua. It covers the right-click half of launcher step 8 (slash-commands §7), which 'Disabled 8' did not test. The case turns the addon off, loads the addon's own tests/mock_menu.lua and right-clicks the launcher with OnClick({}, "RightButton"). It then checks that:
- the menu opens and the settings panel does not;
- Enabled can still be clicked;
- Locked, Test mode and Show window are grayed and do nothing when clicked;
- nothing is written to SavedVariables, no frame is shown and no chat line is printed.

It carries the testing-§12 comment saying what change would make it fail. To check that it can fail, I ran the suite on a scratch copy where the launcher's isEnabled always returned true. The new case failed there with "Locked is not grayed while disabled". No production code changed. I regenerated docs/test-cases.md (the total went from 2197 to 2198) and updated the README Tests badge to 2198/2198. This resolves finding MM-A-08.
